          "email": "jsimmons@infradead.org",
          "date": "2026-10-06 18:34:41.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-18687 llite: cleanup BDI_CAP_* flags",
        "message": "LU-18687 llite: cleanup BDI_CAP_* flags\n\nAccording to git commit v5.9-rc3-156-ged7b6b4f6e91 upstream\nwe don't need BDI_CAP_CGROUP_WRITEBACK anymore for SB_I_CGROUPWB\nto function. For only kernels we need to keep it around. Also\nSB_I_CGROUPWB has been around since 4.1 so we don't need the ifdef\nanymore for SB_I_CGROUPWB.\n\nFor git commit 2841808f35eebfd07150333f3af3007cb2904a09 upstream\nBDI_CAP_WRITEBACK_ACCT was removed. This is only needed for\nwb_stat_mod() handling which is not used by lustre and also was\nremoved upstream. We can remove the wb_stats handling as well.\nBy default the Linux kernel enables a similar type of accounting\nwith newer kernels.\n\nDue to these changes we can greatly simplify Lustre.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nChange-Id: I1417eca54d9fa6b2c0e1d7d8a197146649f0b3c8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
